cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the artifacts, tooling, or measurements in this repository, please cite it (see also paper/references.bib and paper/main_en.md / paper/main_zh.md)."
title: "Verifying, Repairing, and Measuring Compressed Formal Proofs: An Independent Track on the Classical Zero-Free Region in Lean 4"
abstract: "An independent verification, repair and measurement track on the classical de la Vallee Poussin zero-free region for zeta(s) (Lean 4 / Mathlib; reference formalization 21 files, 21,641 normalized tokens). Contributions: a verification pipeline (compile + kernel axiom audit + token measurement calibrated to +/-8 tokens); a repair case study turning a non-compiling 3,179-token work-in-progress into a 3,208-token artifact accepted by official replay (official score 64.64, curve flag kept=true); a measured record of the submitted compressed lineage (2,931-3,315 tokens, official scores 64.47-65.13); an independent Case A/B architecture; and an ablation showing the Euler-Maclaurin growth route costs ~50% more formal tokens than the Mellin route. The compressed proof family and its headline technique were developed by a parallel track in a shared workshop workspace and are reproduced with attribution."
